-- =========================================================================
-- module query where — the LIVE relational-query bridge (solver-extension
-- Phase 4). The thin host-re-entry hop from a production Fenel orchestration
-- body (`state:queryRel`) into the engine's SHIPPED query machinery
-- (`engine:queryRel` / `engine:queryRelOne` = solve ∘ materialize, expr-
-- substrate Phase 16) — run in the engine's CURATED dispatch harness, NOT the
-- production registry.
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- WHY THIS BRIDGE EXISTS (the engine→production exposure, Step-0 finding).
-- The engine query bodies + their transitive closure (rel-solve / solve /
-- reify / materialize / enumerate) call bare `contains` meaning the STRING
-- predicate `std:contains`. The production registry ALSO carries
-- `decidableMembershipModule`, whose `set:contains` publishes the SAME bare
-- codeName; codeName resolution is last-write-wins, so in production bare
-- `contains` resolves to `set:contains` (the set-membership decider). Running
-- the engine query bodies directly in the production registry therefore
-- mis-dispatches `contains` → a `$`-keyed-SetExpr marshal crash. This is the
-- exact shadow the engine's `dispatchEngineBody` harness (`getHarness`,
-- engine-bodies-dispatch.ts) is curated to avoid (it registers a one-function
-- SLICE of decidable-membership, NOT `set:contains`). So a production query
-- must route through that harness — and a Fenel body cannot call
-- `dispatchEngineBody` (host re-entry). This `ffi/` native is that irreducible
-- hop: the SAME engine-dispatch-boundary category as `prover/ffi`'s
-- `decidableSetProposerNative` (a prod module whose ffi natives bridge to
-- engine bodies via `dispatchEngineBody`, "un-portable by definition"). It
-- reuses the SHIPPED `dispatchedQueryRel` / `dispatchedQueryRelOne` wrappers —
-- no new reasoning, no new marshalling, just the dispatch hop. The content
-- gate permits `.ts` under `fenel/modules/` ONLY inside `ffi/`; the impls live
-- in `fenel/modules/query/ffi/query-ffi.ts` and are LEDGERED.
--
-- Inputs are the `$`-free plain records the CALLER (state:queryRel) builds:
--   expr     — the query predicate, an `Expr` value (built by the caller).
--   relDefs  — a list of relDef markers `{ name, fieldOrder, instances }`
--              (the materialize.fenel marker shape; instances = the flat
--              merged-envelope rows `state:listInstancesByName` returns).
--   rules    — a pre-reified rules list (each `{ name, params, body }`).
-- Returns the inherited P15/P16 split: `Just bindings` (findall — possibly
-- `Just []` = safe-but-empty) for `rel`; `Just binding` / `Nothing` (no
-- satisfying row / out-of-fragment) for `relOne`.
--
-- The native passes the markers straight through to the harness, which owns
-- the real shapes. Its boundary still distinguishes the Expr, relDef/rule
-- marker lists, findall binding matrix, and first-witness binding list; one
-- shared `a` would falsely equate those independent carriers.
-- =========================================================================

module query where

@native
@label "Run relational query (findall)"
@description "solver-extension Phase 4 — the live bridge to engine:queryRel (= solveRelAll ∘ factsFromDefs). Materialize the relDef markers + rules into the P13 facts env and enumerate ALL satisfying bindings of the predicate Expr, run inside the engine's curated dispatch harness (NOT the production registry — the std:contains vs set:contains codeName shadow). Returns Just bindings (Just [] = safe-but-empty) or Nothing (out-of-fragment). Host-re-entry ffi native delegating to the shipped dispatchedQueryRel; the prover/ffi engine-dispatch-boundary category."
@tags "query" "solver" "relational" "materialize" "bridge" "phase-4"
@category "query"
@codeName "runRelQuery"
rel : (expr: Expr) -> (relDefs: List ({})) -> (rules: List ({})) -> Maybe (List (List ({})))

@native
@label "Run relational query (first witness)"
@description "solver-extension Phase 4 — the first-witness sibling of query:rel, bridging engine:queryRelOne (= solveRel ∘ factsFromDefs). Materialize the relDef markers + rules into the facts env and return the FIRST satisfying binding (Nothing = out-of-fragment / no satisfying row). Run inside the engine's curated dispatch harness. Host-re-entry ffi native delegating to the shipped dispatchedQueryRelOne."
@tags "query" "solver" "relational" "materialize" "bridge" "phase-4"
@category "query"
@codeName "runRelQueryOne"
relOne : (expr: Expr) -> (relDefs: List ({})) -> (rules: List ({})) -> Maybe (List ({}))
